WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:04.163
You chose a DDoS tier and
named what it doesn't cover.

3
00:00:04.163 --> 00:00:08.724
You checked that every public I P
is protected, logged and alerting.

4
00:00:08.724 --> 00:00:13.537
You took the web application firewall from
detection to prevention, tuned first.

5
00:00:13.537 --> 00:00:17.849
And you proved it blocks a test request,
with the matching row in its log.

6
00:00:17.849 --> 00:00:23.186
The evidence an I S S O keeps from this
module: the plan and its linked networks,

7
00:00:23.186 --> 00:00:27.252
the per-I P mode export, DDoS
metrics, logs and alert history,

8
00:00:27.252 --> 00:00:33.096
the simulation report when the exercise
runs, the firewall policy exports and logs,

9
00:00:33.096 --> 00:00:37.162
the blocked test request, and
the rule-exception register.

10
00:00:37.162 --> 00:00:39.922
Next is Module 3, the edge and the egress:

11
00:00:39.922 --> 00:00:45.770
an origin nothing can reach around Front
Door, and egress through Azure Firewall.
